According to a report by Intel Market Research,  global market for visual effects (VFX) services has entered a transformative phase, buoyed by escalating production budgets, the proliferation of subscription based streaming platforms, and breakthroughs in real time rendering and artificial intelligence assisted workflows. In 2025, VFX services commanded a valuation of USD 28 billion, and the forecast predicts a resilient rise to USD 55 billion by 2034, reflecting an annualised compound growth rate of approximately 8% over the ensuing decade.
